# GSD and Open Dough coexistence

Use GSD for milestones and Open Dough for story and slice delivery. When both
apply, this repository's rules and delivery requirements take precedence over
GSD defaults. Do not enable GSD workflow enforcement that forbids local workflows.

- Keep story seeds in `.planning/seeds/` and executable plans in
  `.planning/phases/` or `.planning/quick/`. Both workflows use the same active
  PLAN; refine it in place. Seeds are not executable.
- Apply [problem decomposition](problem-decomposition.mdc) and the sizing limits
  in `AGENTS.md` to GSD tasks as well as Open Dough slices. Delivery examples
  do not define product architecture or rejection rules.
- Every execution engine must follow
  [dough-execute-plan](../../.agents/skills/dough-execute-plan/SKILL.md)'s slice
  delivery contract: Jidoka, fresh refactor agent, API generation when needed,
  one coordinator-run `./scripts/run.sh pnpm format:changed`, plan update,
  commit, push, and asynchronous CI handling.
- Give each active plan one writer. Parallel work must not overlap files,
  mutable state, or plan writes.
- GSD owns `.planning/STATE.md` as its project index. Open Dough execution
  resumes from the PLAN and does not update that index.
- Retain completed plans and review evidence through
  [dough-execution-retrospective](../../.agents/skills/dough-execution-retrospective/SKILL.md).
  Only afterward use
  [dough-story-wrap-up](../../.agents/skills/dough-story-wrap-up/SKILL.md)
  to assimilate lasting knowledge and remove spent history with Git recovery.
  Finishing the last slice alone does not authorize cleanup.

Other planning scope and lifecycle rules live in [planning.mdc](planning.mdc).
